From 8c32a9a5710807d29d0aa0cf2e9a6f9feef9cfaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@example.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:50:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move Todo Task dashboard filters into a bottom-sheet drawer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Filter icon (FilterListIcon) added to the icon cluster of any section
  with dashboardFilter set (currently just todo_task); icon tints when
  a filter is active.
- Replaces the always-visible inline filter row with a shared MUI
  Drawer (anchor=bottom) opened via filterSheetFor state — same
  Select controls, same applyDashboardFilters/getFilterableFields
  logic as before, just relocated so the card isn't cluttered by
  default.
- Reset/Apply buttons in the sheet; Reset clears that section's
  filtersBySection entry, Apply just closes the sheet (filters already
  applied live via existing state).
- BottomNav.jsx: removed a stale comment that still described the
  'Todo' tab as an unwired placeholder -- the route wiring itself
  (ROUTES[1] -> /todo-task/new -> navigate()) was already correct.
